        "statement": "There are extensive flooding problems throughout Plymouth."
      },
      {
        "stage": 16,
        "statement": "Residential areas and high school property flood. Water from 1 to 3 feet deep affects southern and eastern sections of the city."
      },
      {
        "stage": 15,
        "statement": "Flooding begins of commercial property along Laporte and Garro Streets."
      },
      {
        "stage": 14.5,
        "statement": "The parking lot on Laporte Street begins to flood."
      },
      {
        "stage": 14,
        "statement": "A small trailer park near the Jefferson Street bridge begins to flood."
      },
      {
        "stage": 13.5,
        "statement": "Some residential and commercial properties near the Jefferson Street Bridge begin to flood."
      },
      {
        "stage": 13,
        "statement": "The right bank of the Yellow River overflows with some city streets...low lying county roads and back yards along Laporte Street in Plymouth flooding.  Low lying agricultural areas flood as well."
      }
    ],
